  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoviendo la Integridad y la Transparencia en los Negocios (ProIntegridad)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Promoviendo la Integridad y la Transparencia en los Negocios (ProIntegridad)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mexico):  The purpose of this activity is to promote Mexico&apos;s business and investment environment by increasing integrity and transparency in the public and private sectors. This objective is achieved by: 1) strengthening Mexican oversight and regulatory bodies to monitor and mitigate corruption risks in the areas where public authorities and corporations interact, such as audits, public procurement, licenses and permits; 2) promoting the adoption of corporate integrity programs and materials in small and medium-size enterprises, including toolkits, guidelines, and training components; and 3) increasing the breadth and diversity of civil society organizations engaged in promoting a fair, transparent, and competitive business environment. Through this activity, USAID is leveling the playing field for U.S. and Mexican companies (including their downstream suppliers), as well as advancing the implementation of the United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement (USMCA), at a critical time when both countries seek to leverage nearshoring opportunities in key sectors. The activity contributes to Mexico ICS Objectives 2.1 by reducing opportunities for corruption and impunity. Also, this activity contributes to the following key issues: GEEA; WPS, Anti-Corruption, Strategic Competition with the Government of the PRC, GE/WE, SME, and Trade Capacity Building. USAID will evaluate the distinct effects that anti-corruption policies have on women and vulnerable groups, whether as business owners, supply chain participants, or customers. USAID will also support women&apos;s involvement in public budgetary planning and expenditure activities. Further support will assist companies to comply with new and existing regulations to offset challenges that disproportionately affect women in business, such as developing anti-harassment policies and promoting women participation and leadership in the private sector..</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">(M&#xe9;xico): La actividad ampl&#xed;a los esfuerzos de USAID para promover el entorno empresarial y de inversi&#xf3;n de M&#xe9;xico mediante la implementaci&#xf3;n de herramientas innovadoras para reforzar la integridad y la transparencia en los sectores p&#xfa;blico y privado. Los fondos del a&#xf1;o fiscal 2022 se utilizar&#xe1;n para asistencia t&#xe9;cnica para fortalecer 1) los &#xf3;rganos reguladores y de supervisi&#xf3;n mexicanos para monitorear y mitigar los riesgos de corrupci&#xf3;n en las &#xe1;reas donde interact&#xfa;an las autoridades p&#xfa;blicas y las corporaciones, como inspecciones, adquisiciones p&#xfa;blicas, licencias y permisos; 2) promover la adopci&#xf3;n de programas y materiales de integridad corporativa en peque&#xf1;as y medianas empresas, incluidos kits de herramientas, directrices y componentes de capacitaci&#xf3;n; y, 3) aumentar la amplitud y diversidad de las organizaciones de la sociedad civil comprometidas con la promoci&#xf3;n de un entorno empresarial justo, transparente y competitivo. Durante el pr&#xf3;ximo a&#xf1;o, esta actividad se centrar&#xe1; principalmente en cinco estados prioritarios (Chihuahua, Guanajuato, Jalisco, Nuevo Le&#xf3;n y Sonora) y tres cadenas de suministro cr&#xed;ticas (automotriz, electr&#xf3;nica y construcci&#xf3;n). Estos esfuerzos ayudar&#xe1;n a nivelar el campo de juego para las empresas estadounidenses, incluidos sus proveedores downstream, y las empresas mexicanas, y avanzar&#xe1;n en la implementaci&#xf3;n del Acuerdo entre Estados Unidos, M&#xe9;xico y Canad&#xe1; (T-MEC). La actividad contribuye a los Objetivos 2.1 de la ICS de M&#xe9;xico al reducir las oportunidades de corrupci&#xf3;n e impunidad... .</narrative>
  </description>
